WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.227
Yeah, we're thinking he's back… again… again.

00:00:04.227 --> 00:00:08.820
Following a production delay of approximately&nbsp;
two years amidst complications brought on by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:13.980
the pandemic, "John Wick: Chapter 4" is finally&nbsp;
on the way to theaters, slated for release in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:19.724
March 2023. And the latest footage from the&nbsp;
movie is driving fans of the series wild.

00:00:19.724 --> 00:00:23.340
This next installment in the "John Wick"&nbsp;
franchise will pick up soon after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.940
events of its third chapter, which marked&nbsp;
a significant shift in the relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:31.260
between Keanu Reeves' title character and&nbsp;
the powerful High Table – the organization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.481
that rules over the secret society&nbsp;
of assassins of which he's a part.

00:00:34.481 --> 00:00:38.220
In August of 2022, with the film's&nbsp;
release less than a year away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:42.540
director Chad Stahelski suggested that&nbsp;
the sky's the limit for the John Wick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.660
franchise when it comes to future&nbsp;
movies. According to the filmmaker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.100
the possibility that John could go to space&nbsp;
one day is even on the table. In some series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.309
that would be a "jump the shark" moment.&nbsp;
In this one, it'd probably just be cool.

00:00:54.889 --> 00:00:58.260
Finally, the official trailer for&nbsp;
"John Wick: Chapter 4" premiered on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.220
November 10. While it doesn't happen to&nbsp;
include a sequence set in outer space,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.760
this extended preview nevertheless&nbsp;
suggests a both unpredictable and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.240
extremely exciting adventure on the&nbsp;
horizon. Are we right about that, John?

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.500
"...yeah."

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.840
Following the release of the full trailer,&nbsp;
many reactions from fans put a spotlight on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.520
the franchise's surprising longevity. Many agree&nbsp;
that "John Wick" has yet to wear out its welcome,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.540
despite laying more convoluted mythology&nbsp;
onto the series with each new installment.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:31.440
On YouTube, a number of commenters&nbsp;
shared their delight at the fact that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.580
four films in, the "John Wick" series is&nbsp;
still dramatically compelling. One user wrote,

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.460
…receiving more than 1500&nbsp;
likes from like-minded viewers.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:48.000
Another Youtube commenter left their&nbsp;
own reply on the trailer, saying,

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:55.080
Seemingly in response to comments like&nbsp;
these, another user praised the "John&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:59.340
Wick" fanbase for its widespread sense of&nbsp;
excitement and general lack of negativity.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:04.020
Meanwhile on the primary movie discussion&nbsp;
subreddit, a number of users expressed similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:08.400
sentiments. One user simply commented that they'll&nbsp;
continue watching "John Wick" movies for as long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.300
as they come out. Another compared the "John&nbsp;
Wick" series to the long-running Marvel movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:16.584
which still pack some entertaining punch&nbsp;
despite being a fixture in theaters for years.

00:02:16.778 --> 00:02:21.240
On Twitter too, plenty of fans shared their&nbsp;
thoughts on the full trailer. Not surprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.740
many of the posters agreed with the consensus&nbsp;
that the franchise has yet to decline in quality.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.240
One Twitter user wrote that they plan on seeing&nbsp;
"Chapter 4" without watching any trailers for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.778
the film beforehand, putting their trust&nbsp;
in the high quality of the series thus far.

00:02:33.778 --> 00:02:38.169
Meanwhile, another user posted four screenshots&nbsp;
from the "Chapter 4" trailer with the caption,

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.860
Pop culture writer Richard Newby praised&nbsp;
the "Chapter 4" trailer on Twitter as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.880
saying that like many others, he has yet&nbsp;
to grow tired of the "John Wick" franchise.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.000
YouTuber Brett Kollmann&nbsp;
even went so far as to joke,

00:02:59.951 --> 00:03:03.720
While it's possible that "John Wick: Chapter&nbsp;
4" could disappoint some longtime fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.720
responses thus far are so overwhelmingly positive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.920
we're not sure how it could. It seems&nbsp;
increasingly likely that this next entry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:15.000
in the series won't just clear the high bar set&nbsp;
by its predecessors – it might just raise it.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.820
"Last words, Winston?"

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.620
"Just have fun out there."

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:23.100
"John Wick: Chapter 4" premieres&nbsp;
in theaters on March 24, 2023.

